 "notes": "Curve is the combined envelope (strongest at each mass) of the BGS-5sigma and LRG-5sigma decay-rate limits in Fig. 8 (vector coordinates extracted from e-print file gamma_comp_update.pdf; BGS is the stronger limit up to ~8.3 eV, LRG extends to 12.4 eV). The paper reports upper limits on the two-photon decay rate Gamma(m); converted to g_agamma via the paper's Eq. 5, Gamma = g^2 m^3 / (64 pi), i.e. g = sqrt(64 pi Gamma hbar / m^3) with Gamma in s^-1 -> eV. IMPORTANT: the paper quotes a 5-sigma detection limit on line surface brightness (more conservative than 95% CL; the paper notes this amounts to about a factor-3 shift in Gamma, i.e. ~sqrt(3) in g, relative to the 95% one-sided MUSE/VIMOS curves), so confidence_level=0.95 is nominal only. Central curves used; the shaded +/-30% surface-mass-density systematic band in Fig. 8 is not included. Limit derived from weak-lensing surface mass densities around DESI BGS/LRG galaxies, so no local DM density rescaling applies.",
